  "title": "Prepositions",
  "emoji": "📍",
  "parentNote": "Prepositions show where something is or when something happens. Play a treasure hunt game! \"The toy is UNDER the table, BEHIND the chair, IN the box.\" This makes learning fun and memorable!",
  "learnBullets": [
    "What a **preposition** is — a word that shows position, direction, or time",
    "**Place prepositions**: in, on, under, behind, in front of, beside, between, near",
    "**Time prepositions**: at, in, on",
    "**Direction prepositions**: to, from, into, out of"
  ],
  "learnItFirst": "**What is a Preposition?**\nA preposition is a word that tells us **where** something is, **when** something happens, or **which direction** something goes.\n\n```\nThe cat is ON the table. (where?)\nSchool starts AT 8 o'clock. (when?)\nShe walked TO the park. (direction?)\n```\n\n**Place Prepositions (Where?):**\n\n| Preposition | Meaning | Example |\n|-------------|---------|---------|\n| in | inside something | The ball is **in** the box. |\n| on | touching the top of | The book is **on** the table. |\n| under | below something | The dog is **under** the bed. |\n| behind | at the back of | He hid **behind** the door. |\n| in front of | before something | She stood **in front of** the class. |\n| beside / next to | at the side of | Sit **beside** me. |\n| between | in the middle of two things | The park is **between** two buildings. |\n| near | close to | My house is **near** the school. |\n\n**Time Prepositions (When?):**\n\n| Preposition | Use with | Example |\n|-------------|----------|---------|\n| at | time | **at** 5 o'clock, **at** noon |\n| in | month, year, part of day | **in** June, **in** 2024, **in** the morning |\n| on | day, date | **on** Monday, **on** 15th August |\n\n### 🧠 How to Choose the Right Preposition\n1. **Ask:** Where is it? When is it? Which direction?\n2. **Picture it** in your mind\n3. **Choose** the preposition that matches the picture\n\n---",
